Give the scripts sfall's fake traits and perks, and what else mods call

Fallout Yesterday's traits and perks are made with sfall's fake traits and
perks, which this engine did not have: has_fake_trait alone is in 516 of its
scripts, and the first call ended the player's script at the start of a new
game. Written here from sfall's documented behaviour (sfall itself is GPL):

- set_fake_trait, set_fake_perk, set_selectable_perk, has_fake_trait,
  has_fake_perk, and their _npc metarules for party members: kept in
  sfallgv.sav in sfall's own layout, listed in the Perks folder of the
  character screen, and undone with the rest when that screen is cancelled.
- The perk box: the selectable perks beside the real ones, which
  hide_real_perks can take away, its title (set_perkbox_title), what a perk
  chosen there becomes (perk_add_mode), and clear_selectable_perks.
- set_perk_level_mod, get_perk_available, set_xp_mod, set_hp_per_level_mod,
  set_critter_hit_chance_mod, set_base_hit_chance_mod, set_pipboy_available,
  get_kill_counter, inc_npc_level, get_npc_level, stop_game, resume_game,
  and init_hook as the game_loaded of hook scripts.
- The graphics functions say they are not available, as sfall does outside
  its DirectX 9 modes, and do nothing. Reading, writing or calling into the
  original program's memory reads 0 and does nothing, as sfall does with its
  unsafe opcodes off, where it used to end the script.
- intface_redraw with an argument redraws the interface bar instead of
  ending the script.
- Card titles longer than their buffer are cut short instead of overrunning it.
